Subject: [PATCH] fiq_debugger: close the console-thread lost-wakeup race

wake_up_console_thread() only calls wake_up_process() when
console_thread_running is false.  The console thread, however, only
stores that false value after it has re-observed both kfifo queues
empty and is about to schedule().  A producer (bash writing its prompt,
or any tty_write burst) that enqueues data in the window between the
thread's emptiness check and the running=false store gets its wakeup
skipped, and the thread then sleeps with a non-empty fifo.  The serial
console stalls until some later event - typically a keystroke whose
echo travels through fiq_tty_write - finally wakes the thread, which
then flushes the whole backlog at once.

This is visible on affected images as prompts that only print their
first few characters and command output that appears in one burst
after pressing Enter several times.

Re-check the fifos after publishing running=false and resume draining
instead of sleeping when new data arrived in the window.  A producer
that arrives after the store still performs wake_up_process() itself,
so no wakeup is lost either way.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/rk_fiq_debugger.c	2026-08-27 16:51:04.820538083 +0800
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/rk_fiq_debugger.c	2026-08-27 16:51:04.843696924 +0800
@@ -359,6 +359,21 @@
 		set_current_state(TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE);
 		if (console_thread_stop || (kfifo_is_empty(&fifo) && kfifo_is_empty(&tty_fifo))) {
 			smp_store_mb(console_thread_running, false);
+			/*
+			 * wake_up_console_thread() skips the wakeup while
+			 * console_thread_running is true, so a producer that
+			 * queued data between the emptiness check above and
+			 * this store would never wake us (lost wakeup): the
+			 * console then stalls until the next input event
+			 * re-echoes through the tty.  Re-check the fifos after
+			 * publishing the false value and keep draining if new
+			 * data arrived; a producer landing after the store
+			 * still takes the wake_up_process() path itself.
+			 */
+			if (unlikely(!kfifo_is_empty(&fifo) || !kfifo_is_empty(&tty_fifo))) {
+				smp_store_mb(console_thread_running, true);
+				continue;
+			}
 			schedule();
 			smp_store_mb(console_thread_running, true);
 		}
